  "description": "Waffling your leftover mashed potatoes gives them a second life that may be even better than their first. The waffle iron crisps the ridges of the potatoes and leaves divots for gravy or other sauces to pool.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: leftover made fluffy mashed potatoes → freshly made fluffy mashed potatoes\n\nNotes: The recipe will work in either a Belgian or standard-style waffle iron.\nIf the Thanksgiving leftover spirit moves you, replace about 1/2 cup of the mashed potatoes with stuffing. The bacon may be swapped out for an equivalent amount of cooked, crumbled sausage.",
